Tired of sending the same four operators on every mission? With [b]Off Duty[/b], operators [b]get tired from back-to-back deployments[/b] and [b]recover while they're off duty[/b], so the rest of your company gets a chance to shine.

[heading]How It Works[/heading]
[list]
[*][b]Every mission adds fatigue[/b] to each operator who deploys (2 by default).[/*]
[*][b]Every strategy turn off duty removes some[/b] (1 by default). Operators away on an operation neither gain nor recover.[/*]
[*][b]Your call, always[/b]: fatigue sets a tier for the next mission, but you can always deploy anyone. A tired operator just fights worse.[/*]
[*][b]Story-safe[/b]: when a mission can't launch without someone, they go in at the tier for [b]half[/b] their fatigue. Their fatigue itself isn't changed.[/*]
[*][b]No surprises[/b]: every squad slot shows a banner (RESTED, REQUIRED, TIRED, EXHAUSTED or SPENT). Hover it for the fatigue, the exact penalties and how long until they're rested. Roster portraits mark anyone tired or required.[/*]
[*][b]Visible in the mission[/b]: the tier shows as a debuff under the health bar and in the Inspect panel, and the hit chance penalty appears in the hit breakdown as "Penalty from Operation".[/*]
[*][b]Separate from injuries[/b]: the game's own injuries work exactly as before.[/*]
[/list]

[heading]Tiers[/heading]
[list]
[*][b]Tired[/b] (Easy 3–4, Standard 2–3, Hard 1–2): −5% hit chance, −5% max health[/*]
[*][b]Exhausted[/b] (Easy 5–6, Standard 4–5, Hard 3–4): −10% hit chance, −10% max health, 10% chance each turn to lose 1 AP[/*]
[*][b]Spent[/b] (Easy 7, Standard 6–7, Hard 5–7): −20% hit chance, −20% max health, −10% movement, 15% chance each turn to lose 1 AP[/*]
[/list]
Numbers were tuned with AI-vs-AI simulations of hundreds of missions.

[heading]Settings[/heading]
With the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starwarszerocompany/mods/149]Mixamoo Mod Config Manager[/url] installed, Off Duty has an in-game settings page:
[list]
[*][b]Preset[/b]: Easy (tiers at 3 / 5 / 7), Standard (2 / 4 / 6, the default) or Hard (1 / 3 / 5); fatigue caps at 7[/*]
[*][b]Fatigue per mission[/b]: 0–4[/*]
[*][b]Recovery per turn off duty[/b]: 0–3[/*]
[*][b]AP loss[/b]: on or off[/*]
[/list]
Without it, Off Duty uses the defaults (Standard, 2, 1, AP loss on).

[heading]Requirements[/heading]
[list]
[*][b]Star Wars Zero Company[/b][/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starwarszerocompany/mods/9]UE4SS for Star Wars Zero Company[/url][/*]
[*]Optional: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starwarszerocompany/mods/149]Mixamoo Mod Config Manager[/url], for the settings page[/*]
[/list]

[heading]Installation[/heading]
The download has two parts, and [b]both are needed[/b]: [b]OffDuty[/b] (the mod) and [b]OffDuty_Assets[/b] (its gameplay effects and status tags).

[b]Mod manager[/b]
Both parts carry metadata for the community mod managers:
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starwarszerocompany/mods/29]Zero Mod Manager[/url]: choose [b]Install all components[/b].[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starwarszerocompany/mods/121]Zero Company Mod Command[/url]: it adds Off Duty and Off Duty — Assets as two entries.[/*]
[/list]
Make sure both are enabled.

[b]Manual installation[/b]
Make sure UE4SS is installed and working, and close the game.
[list=1]
[*]Extract the [b]OffDuty[/b] folder into:
[code]SWZeroCompany/Binaries/Win64/ue4ss/Mods/[/code][/*]
[*]Copy the three files inside [b]OffDuty_Assets[/b] ([b]OffDuty_P.pak[/b], [b]OffDuty_P.ucas[/b], [b]OffDuty_P.utoc[/b]) into (create [b]~mods[/b] if it's missing):
[code]SWZeroCompany/Content/Paks/~mods/[/code][/*]
[/list]
The package includes [b]enabled.txt[/b]. If your UE4SS setup doesn't pick it up, add this line to [b]ue4ss/Mods/mods.txt[/b]:
[code]OffDuty : 1[/code]
[b]Updating:[/b] close the game first, then install the new ZIP the same way.

[b]Uninstalling[/b]
Switch both parts off or remove them in your mod manager, or delete the [b]OffDuty[/b] folder and the three [b]OffDuty_P[/b] files. Saves stay loadable; operators simply stop tiring.

[heading]Known Issues[/heading]
[list]
[*]Restart the game after installing or updating Off Duty. Don't use UE4SS's "Reload All Mods"; it can crash or freeze the game.[/*]
[*]Guest units who aren't on your roster (such as Rex) don't gain fatigue.[/*]
[/list]

[heading]Troubleshooting[/heading]
Off Duty writes diagnostic information to [b]off_duty.log[/b] in its [b]OffDuty[/b] folder. [b]UE4SS.log[/b] remains the primary startup and crash log.
When reporting a problem, please include:
[list]
[*]Your game build[/*]
[*]Your UE4SS version[/*]
[*]Your other installed mods[/*]
[*]What you were doing and what happened[/*]
[*][code]UE4SS.log[/code] and [code]off_duty.log[/code][/*]
[/list]
The logs only contain technical details about what the mod did: no screenshots, saves or personal files. They may mention folder paths on your PC, so feel free to look them over before sending.

[heading]Source Code and Issue Reports[/heading]
Source, technical documentation and issue tracking are available on [url=https://github.com/chatterchats/ZComOffDuty]GitHub[/url]. You can also post in the Bugs tab here on Nexus.

